WEBVTT

00:32.949 --> 00:34.826
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:48.525 --> 01:50.068
Izutsumi, Chilchuck...

01:51.277 --> 01:52.946
Could you slow down a bit?

01:53.488 --> 01:55.657
Cracks are all over the floor,
and it's hard to walk.

01:56.658 --> 01:58.409
I didn't notice.

01:59.452 --> 02:00.829
Let's take a break.

02:02.413 --> 02:04.082
What is this? An old folks' stroll?

02:05.625 --> 02:07.794
Something's bothering me.

02:07.877 --> 02:08.837
In our current forms,

02:08.920 --> 02:12.298
how different are our actual ages
from how old we look?

02:12.924 --> 02:15.009
Laios, how old are you now?

02:15.510 --> 02:16.761
I'm 26.

02:17.303 --> 02:20.348
Senshi, how old
does Laios look to you now?

02:21.724 --> 02:23.351
Around 60, maybe?

02:23.434 --> 02:27.147
<i>They say a dwarf lives
2.5 times longer than a tall-man.</i>

02:27.230 --> 02:29.315
<i>So 26 years for a tall-man...</i>

02:30.108 --> 02:31.943
<i>is like 65 for a dwarf.</i>

02:32.443 --> 02:36.114
<i>So, our appearance
reflects our actual age.</i>

02:36.698 --> 02:39.075
What really concerns me
is our remaining lifespan.

02:39.576 --> 02:42.370
Do we age at the same pace
as before our transformation,

02:42.453 --> 02:44.873
or do we age according to our new forms?

02:45.874 --> 02:49.335
Marcille, you act like
this is none of your concern.

02:49.419 --> 02:50.795
But if the latter is true,

02:50.879 --> 02:54.132
the average lifespan
for us half-foots is 50!

02:54.215 --> 02:58.219
In less than 40 years,
you'll be all wrinkled and die!

02:58.303 --> 02:59.429
What?!

03:00.597 --> 03:02.265
WRINKLECILLE

03:02.348 --> 03:04.642
Is the lifespan really that short?

03:04.726 --> 03:06.728
I thought you could live until 100.

03:06.811 --> 03:08.396
Some do, but...

03:08.479 --> 03:09.772
It's only a small percentage.

03:15.778 --> 03:17.280
I was just joking.

03:17.363 --> 03:22.076
My point is, if that's true,
these mushrooms are too convenient.

03:22.577 --> 03:26.080
There are loads of people who would pay
a fortune to change their race,

03:26.164 --> 03:28.791
but I've never seen those mushrooms
for sale anywhere.

03:28.875 --> 03:31.377
<i>In other words, this transformation
must be temporary,</i>

03:31.461 --> 03:33.129
<i>or it comes with nasty side effects.</i>

03:34.047 --> 03:35.173
Side effects, huh?

03:35.757 --> 03:37.050
That's a possibility.

03:37.133 --> 03:39.552
I was hoping
we could make use of it somehow,

03:39.636 --> 03:41.471
but I guess it's not that simple.

03:41.554 --> 03:42.972
Make use of it how?

03:43.056 --> 03:44.974
Do you want to become
a demi-human or something?

03:45.058 --> 03:46.559
T-That's not it.

03:46.643 --> 03:49.812
I was thinking about Falin.

03:49.896 --> 03:51.147
Falin?

03:51.231 --> 03:53.358
This is just a what-if, but...

03:53.441 --> 03:56.569
Say everything works out, and we manage
to defeat the lunatic magician.

03:57.487 --> 03:58.947
I repent.

03:59.030 --> 04:00.323
<i>Falin regains herself.</i>

04:01.658 --> 04:03.409
What have I been doing?

04:03.493 --> 04:04.577
- Hurray!
- Hurray!

04:05.078 --> 04:06.246
<i>We return to the surface.</i>

04:06.329 --> 04:08.206
Honestly, we had such a rough time!

04:09.707 --> 04:11.084
<i>People will be terrified.</i>

04:11.668 --> 04:12.585
Right?

04:12.669 --> 04:16.089
I think it'll be tough for her
to remain a dragon from the waist down.

04:16.172 --> 04:17.340
- You stupid--
- Hold on!

04:17.423 --> 04:18.800
Let's hear him out.

04:19.300 --> 04:22.303
<i>I've thought of hiding the lower part
of her body inside a hole.</i>

04:22.387 --> 04:23.346
Welcome!

04:23.429 --> 04:24.472
<i>However,</i>

04:24.973 --> 04:28.977
a large monster can't survive
in a village with little mana.

04:29.602 --> 04:32.438
Just like a fish can't survive
outside of water,

04:32.522 --> 04:35.358
Falin might not be able
to survive in a village.

04:36.276 --> 04:37.485
And that's where

04:37.568 --> 04:40.655
those Changeling mushrooms come into play.

04:41.531 --> 04:45.743
<i>If we can somehow change
her lower body to a smaller dragon,</i>

04:46.286 --> 04:49.080
Falin might be able to live comfortably
in a human village!

04:49.580 --> 04:52.292
- What--
- What an optimistic guy!

04:52.375 --> 04:53.501
Mušḫuššu!

04:53.584 --> 04:57.505
Well, I won't deny
that I also have a wish to transform.

04:57.588 --> 05:01.301
Tall-men are just
so unremarkable and dull...

05:01.384 --> 05:04.012
Hey, don't you hear that strange noise?

05:04.095 --> 05:07.140
No. It's probably
the sound of dwarf relics.

05:07.223 --> 05:08.349
It's not that.

05:08.975 --> 05:10.893
It sounds like rocks
striking against each other.

05:11.477 --> 05:14.522
And it seems like
it's slowly getting closer.

05:16.482 --> 05:17.317
I know.

05:18.026 --> 05:19.861
Gargoyles!

05:20.361 --> 05:23.031
Didn't you close the door properly?

05:23.114 --> 05:24.907
W-We need to get out of here quickly!

05:25.491 --> 05:27.160
They're getting closer!

05:27.869 --> 05:30.621
If we don't do something,
they'll keep coming after us.

05:31.122 --> 05:33.458
We should ambush them.

05:34.375 --> 05:35.418
B-But...

05:35.501 --> 05:37.003
I'll distract the enemies.

05:37.086 --> 05:38.338
Chilchuck, hold the pot.

05:38.421 --> 05:40.173
Izutsumi, slip around behind them.

05:40.256 --> 05:41.841
Senshi, wait for the right moment.

05:41.924 --> 05:43.468
Marcille, how close are the enemies?

05:43.551 --> 05:44.552
Like I said,

05:44.635 --> 05:46.304
they're right there!

05:49.265 --> 05:50.308
Laios!

05:52.518 --> 05:53.644
Damn it!

05:54.270 --> 05:55.772
Everyone, watch out!

06:01.527 --> 06:05.073
Do you get why the first thing I do
is take cover?

06:05.156 --> 06:06.866
Don't hang around our feet.

06:06.949 --> 06:08.451
Easier said than done...

06:08.534 --> 06:10.787
Forget it! You're still as clumsy as ever.

06:10.870 --> 06:11.788
Come here!

06:16.334 --> 06:17.752
What is this smoke?

06:18.586 --> 06:20.004
Is it one of your magic?

06:21.089 --> 06:22.590
Are you two hurt?

06:22.673 --> 06:25.134
No! The sword
just passed between our arms!

06:25.218 --> 06:26.094
Good.

06:26.177 --> 06:27.678
Pass me Kensuke, would you?

06:27.762 --> 06:28.596
Sure.

06:32.100 --> 06:33.726
Did it always look like that?

06:33.810 --> 06:34.769
Nope.

06:34.852 --> 06:36.395
Has the shape of the sword changed?

06:36.938 --> 06:39.023
Was that smoke...

06:39.857 --> 06:42.151
- Spores from Changelings?
- Spores from Changelings?

06:42.235 --> 06:45.780
B-But I don't see
a ring of mushrooms anywhere.

06:45.863 --> 06:48.282
It passed through a circle
we formed with our arms.

06:49.867 --> 06:51.119
Does that mean...

06:58.000 --> 06:59.544
They keep flying away!

06:59.627 --> 07:00.545
Everyone!

07:00.628 --> 07:03.297
Hold hands and make a ring right now!

07:03.381 --> 07:05.133
Read the situation before you say that!

07:05.216 --> 07:06.259
I did!

07:09.220 --> 07:10.054
Now what?

07:10.138 --> 07:12.181
What do we do?

07:12.265 --> 07:15.059
We'll get a Gargoyle
to pass through our ring.

07:15.143 --> 07:16.936
If my guess is correct,

07:17.019 --> 07:19.605
the Gargoyle will transform!

07:20.898 --> 07:22.525
Here it comes! Dodge!

07:22.608 --> 07:24.735
There's a wall on that side! This way!

07:24.819 --> 07:25.778
Ow!

07:25.862 --> 07:28.531
I'll tear in two!

07:31.617 --> 07:33.536
Owie.

07:44.130 --> 07:45.798
It's stuck!

07:45.882 --> 07:47.300
Now, surround it quickly!

07:56.684 --> 07:58.936
We did it! Where's the Gargoyle?

07:59.437 --> 08:00.313
Look!

08:03.065 --> 08:04.692
That's the Gargoyle?

08:05.193 --> 08:06.861
It really transformed!

08:06.944 --> 08:09.363
I see. The Changelings caused this.

08:10.031 --> 08:12.325
So nonliving things change faster.

08:13.326 --> 08:14.243
Laios!

08:14.327 --> 08:15.369
Are you okay?

08:15.453 --> 08:17.371
It hurts, but I'll manage.

08:17.455 --> 08:20.082
Dwarves have sturdy bodies.

08:20.166 --> 08:21.125
Damn it.

08:23.711 --> 08:25.922
That one won't come down.

08:26.005 --> 08:28.633
How can we get it
to pass through our arms?

08:33.221 --> 08:34.305
- Marcille.
- Huh?

08:34.388 --> 08:35.806
- Give me your hand for a bit.
- Huh?

08:39.227 --> 08:40.978
- It should work.
- Um.

08:41.062 --> 08:42.438
- Let's do it.
- All right!

08:42.980 --> 08:45.107
We're going to get up close to it,

08:45.650 --> 08:47.276
and provoke it into attacking us!

08:47.360 --> 08:49.570
- Hey, what do I--
- Run in sync with the call!

08:49.654 --> 08:50.947
Here we go!

08:51.030 --> 08:55.201
- One, two...
- One, two...

08:55.284 --> 09:01.082
- One, two...
- One, two...

09:03.167 --> 09:05.253
Here it comes! Are you ready?

09:05.336 --> 09:06.837
Ready for what?!

09:06.921 --> 09:08.673
- Ready, set...
- Ready, set...

09:08.756 --> 09:10.591
Fly, Marcille!

09:25.731 --> 09:26.816
It's over.

09:28.734 --> 09:29.944
There was nothing to it.

09:30.444 --> 09:34.365
All we had to do was wash the spores
off our bodies to turn back.

09:35.199 --> 09:36.742
It feels wrong.

09:36.826 --> 09:38.786
Don't worry about it. It's just water.

09:38.869 --> 09:40.871
You should wash them off thoroughly.

09:40.955 --> 09:43.624
Right now, we're like
seedbeds for mushrooms.

09:45.209 --> 09:48.671
<i>Now I understand why those mushrooms
have this characteristic.</i>

09:50.214 --> 09:53.092
<i>When animals have their forms
changed by Changelings...</i>

09:53.593 --> 09:54.427
- Run!
- Run!

09:54.510 --> 09:56.012
<i>They're hated by their own kind.</i>

09:56.637 --> 09:57.680
<i>They die.</i>

09:57.763 --> 10:00.266
<i>And they become new Changelings.</i>

10:00.349 --> 10:02.184
It's quite the side effect.

10:02.685 --> 10:06.606
Unlike Gargoyles,
it'll take time for us to turn back.

10:07.106 --> 10:08.983
Let's prepare a meal as we wait.

10:10.318 --> 10:11.444
Of course.

10:15.031 --> 10:18.200
<i>Kensuke, look at how you've changed.</i>

10:18.868 --> 10:23.623
<i>I doubt it was the mushrooms
that turned the insides into a key, but...</i>

10:24.123 --> 10:26.417
<i>Will it revert if I give it a wash?</i>

10:29.545 --> 10:30.671
What are we having today?

10:30.755 --> 10:34.091
We still have some dumplings left,
so we'll boil them.

10:34.175 --> 10:35.426
That again.

10:35.509 --> 10:37.470
Do you have a problem?

10:37.553 --> 10:39.555
Not really. I'm just tired of them.

10:40.514 --> 10:43.309
- <i>Tired of them?</i>
- She sure is a free spirit.

10:45.019 --> 10:46.646
<i>I'll try cooking them differently.</i>

10:48.064 --> 10:52.360
<i>Heat oil in a pan,
and gently place the dumplings in it.</i>

10:52.902 --> 10:54.320
H-Hot!

10:54.904 --> 10:58.908
<i>When the wrappers are golden brown,
take them out and let the oil drain.</i>

10:59.408 --> 11:01.994
<i>Izutsumi is a light eater</i>

11:02.078 --> 11:04.413
<i>and never touches something
she doesn't like.</i>

11:04.914 --> 11:08.751
<i>To make sure she eats enough,
I have to put in the time and effort.</i>

11:12.254 --> 11:14.423
What do you think, Izutsumi?

11:15.049 --> 11:16.425
You just fried them?

11:17.218 --> 11:18.135
Stop that!

11:23.015 --> 11:24.183
<i>Just maybe...</i>

11:30.523 --> 11:32.316
It changed its shape!

11:32.400 --> 11:35.986
Just as I thought,
it seems like the mouth acts as a ring.

11:36.070 --> 11:38.989
And there are so many
varieties of dumplings.

11:39.073 --> 11:42.701
What if I eat one and end up
growing mushrooms in my stomach?

11:43.285 --> 11:47.081
We had the Hippogriff's meat,
and that didn't happen.

11:47.164 --> 11:48.707
Digestion is quite powerful.

11:48.791 --> 11:51.794
Now, help set the dishes.

11:52.545 --> 11:53.796
It's done!

11:53.879 --> 11:56.465
DUMPLINGS TRANSFORMED
BY A CHANGELING FAIRY RING

11:56.549 --> 11:58.342
There are so many types.

12:03.556 --> 12:05.933
This one has Barometz meat in it.

12:06.016 --> 12:07.643
Mutton, huh?

12:08.144 --> 12:09.728
So the filling changes too.

12:11.188 --> 12:12.440
This one's got cheese inside!

12:12.940 --> 12:14.233
This one's sweet.

12:15.025 --> 12:17.153
<i>What meat is this?</i>

12:24.452 --> 12:26.829
Your legs are just too long!

12:29.498 --> 12:31.584
My body's back to normal!

12:31.667 --> 12:32.626
Damn it.

12:32.710 --> 12:34.378
What an awful way to wake up.

12:34.462 --> 12:36.172
Thank goodness.

12:36.255 --> 12:38.007
I'm so glad.

12:38.090 --> 12:41.051
Well then, we should get going soon.

12:41.594 --> 12:44.263
You should change into something lighter.

12:44.346 --> 12:46.348
This floor is warm.

12:47.349 --> 12:50.644
The temperature is conducive
to creature reproduction.

12:50.728 --> 12:55.357
But I'm not sure if there are any living
things ahead in this environment.

12:55.983 --> 12:59.278
I should have made sausages or something.

12:59.361 --> 13:02.865
Speaking of which,
didn't you make some with Red Dragon meat?

13:04.033 --> 13:04.909
<i>I did.</i>

13:04.992 --> 13:06.076
BONELESS DRAGON HAM

13:06.160 --> 13:08.204
But I lost them.

13:08.287 --> 13:09.580
Is that so?

13:09.663 --> 13:10.831
Never mind.

13:11.415 --> 13:13.459
I don't like it when it's hot.

13:15.419 --> 13:17.713
Why is your sword wrapped in a cloth?

13:17.796 --> 13:19.882
Huh? That's because...

13:19.965 --> 13:21.175
Show me.

13:21.258 --> 13:23.135
No, I can't do that.

13:23.219 --> 13:24.345
Show me!

13:26.472 --> 13:27.973
What should we do with him?

13:28.474 --> 13:31.018
Should we form a ring around him
and beat him up?

13:31.894 --> 13:33.812
Go wash it off right now.

13:36.440 --> 13:37.733
How are things over there?

13:38.234 --> 13:40.110
All I see is a strange building.

13:40.194 --> 13:41.904
I don't see any other paths.

13:45.366 --> 13:46.617
A strange building?

13:50.746 --> 13:53.165
It's probably an automatic trolley.

13:53.249 --> 13:55.042
Let's take a peek inside.

13:58.671 --> 14:00.923
I bet it won't move anymore.

14:01.507 --> 14:04.552
If you dismantle it and sell it,
you can fetch a pretty good price.

14:08.305 --> 14:09.431
It moved!

14:09.515 --> 14:11.684
Senshi, what did you do?

14:11.767 --> 14:12.977
Nothing.

14:13.060 --> 14:16.230
Maybe it's the type that moves
when someone boards it.

14:16.814 --> 14:19.066
There's a description here,
so I'll read it.

14:19.567 --> 14:20.943
Take a seat.

14:36.584 --> 14:39.503
There isn't much written here.

14:39.587 --> 14:42.840
It doesn't feel dangerous so far,

14:42.923 --> 14:45.217
so let's ride it as far as it goes.

14:49.096 --> 14:50.598
Maybe I'll brew some tea.

14:52.099 --> 14:53.475
What's that?

14:53.559 --> 14:56.353
Roasted Dryad seeds.

14:56.437 --> 14:58.188
Is the magic circle ready?

14:58.272 --> 14:59.273
I think so.

14:59.857 --> 15:02.610
I can't say for sure if it's working.

15:05.446 --> 15:07.948
It's slow, but it seems to be heating up.

15:08.574 --> 15:09.992
By the way, Laios,

15:10.492 --> 15:13.787
why did you and your sister
become adventurers?

15:13.871 --> 15:15.581
Huh? Me?

15:15.664 --> 15:18.834
You don't strike me as someone
who dreams of making a fortune.

15:20.336 --> 15:22.463
It's a long story, but...

15:23.756 --> 15:27.509
<i>When I was in my teens,
I got fed up with my village.</i>

15:27.593 --> 15:30.262
<i>And I went to a school in the town
and joined the army.</i>

15:31.597 --> 15:34.266
<i>But in the end,
I didn't fit in there either.</i>

15:34.350 --> 15:37.436
<i>And I got picked up by a caravan
that passed through the town.</i>

15:38.020 --> 15:39.146
<i>So he's a deserter?</i>

15:40.397 --> 15:43.317
<i>I slowly drifted south,
taking odd jobs along the way.</i>

15:45.361 --> 15:48.364
<i>Falin was boarding
at a nearby magic school,</i>

15:48.447 --> 15:50.532
<i>so I dropped by to see her.</i>

15:50.616 --> 15:52.868
<i>But she insisted on joining me.</i>

15:56.580 --> 15:58.999
<i>And together, we reached this island.</i>

16:00.376 --> 16:03.879
<i>When we first arrived on this island,
gold-peeling was thriving.</i>

16:03.963 --> 16:05.798
<i>And there was plenty of escorting work.</i>

16:06.924 --> 16:10.511
<i>Then, we just stayed
and hung around the dungeon.</i>

16:21.772 --> 16:23.065
That's how I ended up here.

16:24.024 --> 16:27.444
What a complete lack of foresight.

16:27.528 --> 16:31.073
You're one thing, but why did you
let your sister go with you?

16:31.156 --> 16:33.867
She could've had a better life at school.

16:36.036 --> 16:39.415
<i>Falin's childhood wasn't very fortunate.</i>

16:39.915 --> 16:42.209
<i>She had a talent for magic,
which she was shunned for.</i>

16:43.794 --> 16:46.338
<i>I couldn't stand the environment.</i>

16:46.422 --> 16:48.757
<i>So I left the village
a year before she did.</i>

16:49.675 --> 16:52.011
<i>Until she entered the magic school, no,</i>

16:52.678 --> 16:54.346
<i>until she met Marcille,</i>

16:54.430 --> 16:56.473
<i>she had her meals all alone.</i>

16:57.808 --> 17:00.686
It breaks my heart to think about it.

17:02.312 --> 17:06.191
Well, Falin's spirit
was much stronger than mine,

17:06.275 --> 17:08.986
so maybe it didn't bother her too much.

17:09.695 --> 17:13.866
But that's why I made a promise to myself
to never abandon her again.

17:13.949 --> 17:17.828
At least, not until someone else shows up
whom she wants to be with.

17:26.462 --> 17:28.005
What the heck? Gross!

17:29.214 --> 17:30.174
Falin...

17:30.841 --> 17:33.594
used to bring me a lot of things.

17:34.678 --> 17:37.097
<i>Strange nuts.</i>

17:37.181 --> 17:39.058
<i>And odd plants.</i>

17:39.767 --> 17:42.686
<i>I've always wondered
why she kept bringing them to me, but...</i>

17:43.771 --> 17:46.023
She probably wanted
to eat them with you, Marcille.

18:05.751 --> 18:06.919
I can't wait...

18:07.419 --> 18:09.713
to share meals with her again.

18:11.173 --> 18:12.633
You'll be able to soon.

18:14.259 --> 18:15.928
The way I see it,

18:16.011 --> 18:18.764
Falin is like bacon and eggs right now.

18:19.264 --> 18:22.935
We once compared souls to eggs.

18:23.018 --> 18:25.729
<i>A sunny side up rests on top
of strips of bacon.</i>

18:25.813 --> 18:29.942
<i>They're stuck together, but it looks like
we can peel them apart nicely.</i>

18:30.025 --> 18:31.735
<i>That's Falin.</i>

18:32.361 --> 18:34.363
Compared to that,
Izutsumi is more like an omelet

18:34.446 --> 18:35.948
with ingredients mixed inside.

18:36.031 --> 18:40.202
<i>With effort, you might be able
to remove the ingredients,</i>

18:40.285 --> 18:43.914
<i>but it's easy to imagine
the egg getting broken up.</i>

18:44.414 --> 18:46.625
So, in Izutsumi's case,

18:46.708 --> 18:51.213
we'll have to find a more careful
and complicated approach.

18:51.713 --> 18:53.465
In other words,

18:53.966 --> 18:56.468
<i>if we cut off the dragon waist down,</i>

18:56.552 --> 18:58.971
<i>can we turn Falin back
into her human form?</i>

18:59.555 --> 19:01.974
It's not that simple, is it?

19:02.474 --> 19:03.600
That day,

19:03.684 --> 19:06.937
I preserved some of the Dragon meat,

19:07.020 --> 19:12.192
but it all turned back into flesh
and merged with Falin.

19:12.776 --> 19:16.697
<i>On the other hand, some of the meat
didn't turn back into a dragon.</i>

19:17.281 --> 19:20.367
It's the parts that we ate at dinner.

19:21.326 --> 19:25.831
Meat that has been digested
by other creatures loses its identity.

19:25.914 --> 19:29.501
This is the only clear law in this dungeon

19:29.585 --> 19:32.671
where the line
between life and death is blurred.

19:33.463 --> 19:37.467
In that case,
if we consume all the dragon parts,

19:37.551 --> 19:42.014
we may be able to drive out
the soul of the dragon.

19:45.267 --> 19:47.060
Y-You know,

19:47.686 --> 19:49.771
I'm surprised
to hear that from you, Senshi.

19:50.439 --> 19:52.983
I thought you were against
that sort of thing.

19:53.066 --> 19:56.278
I'm still against resurrecting people.

19:56.904 --> 19:59.907
However, Falin is alive now.

19:59.990 --> 20:04.786
And you just want to release her
from the dungeon.

20:05.370 --> 20:08.040
I'll gladly help you with that.

20:09.583 --> 20:11.793
Eat the dragon parts.

20:12.377 --> 20:15.130
B-But...

20:16.506 --> 20:18.842
how many meals would that make?

20:18.926 --> 20:20.552
- That's your problem?
- That's your problem?

20:20.636 --> 20:21.970
What else would it be?

20:22.054 --> 20:24.598
It's the most promising method
we've got so far!

20:24.681 --> 20:26.600
Do you have a better idea?

20:26.683 --> 20:30.270
Consuming a creature you've killed
to make it your own.

20:30.354 --> 20:32.606
Why didn't I realize it sooner?

20:32.689 --> 20:35.359
It's what we've been doing all along!

20:36.235 --> 20:38.779
But it's massive.

20:39.321 --> 20:42.241
<i>Even if the five of us push
to consume a kilogram each day,</i>

20:42.324 --> 20:44.368
<i>it'll still take us
over a decade to finish it all.</i>

20:45.077 --> 20:47.788
Do you honestly think
I can handle eating a kilogram?

20:47.871 --> 20:51.625
And considering Falin's condition,
we definitely don't have time for that.

20:51.708 --> 20:55.379
So, just ask others to help.

20:55.963 --> 20:59.216
It's time to make full use
of the connections you've built.

20:59.716 --> 21:01.885
You're banking on my connections for this?

21:02.427 --> 21:04.263
It's not like you're without any.

21:04.346 --> 21:06.223
Can't you think of anyone?

21:08.308 --> 21:09.393
<i>The orcs.</i>

21:09.476 --> 21:12.145
<i>They'll likely eat a fair amount
and seem like a promising choice.</i>

21:12.229 --> 21:14.314
<i>The inhabitants of the Golden Castle.</i>

21:14.398 --> 21:17.025
<i>They might not have
the heartiest appetite,</i>

21:17.109 --> 21:19.653
<i>but their numbers and livestock
can compensate for that.</i>

21:19.736 --> 21:22.364
<i>Then there's Namari, Shuro,
and their groups.</i>

21:22.447 --> 21:24.908
<i>Those two will lend a hand
if we appeal to their emotions.</i>

21:24.992 --> 21:28.287
<i>And Kabru seemed interested
in trying monster food.</i>

21:28.996 --> 21:31.915
That's all I can come up with
at the moment.

21:32.416 --> 21:34.042
That's quite a list.

21:34.126 --> 21:36.169
But we're hardly enough
to consume the entire dragon.

21:36.253 --> 21:38.964
I wish we could also have another troop.

21:39.047 --> 21:40.340
But at least

21:40.924 --> 21:43.343
we've got clear goals now.

21:45.262 --> 21:49.182
<i>First, we release the Winged Lion
from the heart of the dungeon.</i>

21:49.266 --> 21:50.183
<i>Second,</i>

21:50.976 --> 21:54.187
<i>with the Lion's aid, we neutralize
the lunatic magician's power.</i>

21:54.271 --> 21:55.188
<i>Third,</i>

21:55.856 --> 21:59.526
<i>we recruit people to assist us
in consuming Falin's dragon parts.</i>

22:00.277 --> 22:02.362
I'm suddenly
feeling optimistic about this.

22:02.946 --> 22:05.324
It's going to be one extravagant feast.

22:05.407 --> 22:08.076
There are no troops inside the dungeon.

22:10.162 --> 22:11.747
What's this sickening feeling?

22:12.247 --> 22:14.958
The air in the dungeon is stale.

22:15.042 --> 22:18.628
While you guys were inside,
it underwent another big transformation.

22:18.712 --> 22:20.047
A transformation?

22:20.130 --> 22:21.673
You'll get it once you see it.

22:22.174 --> 22:25.469
Well, it's going to be
an unpleasant transformation

22:25.552 --> 22:27.637
for the folks behind us, at least.

22:38.398 --> 22:39.733
Don't eat stuff like that!

22:41.818 --> 22:43.862
What's all this racket?

22:45.655 --> 22:47.240
<i>Walking Mushrooms.</i>

22:47.824 --> 22:50.452
How about using them
as a garnish for a steak

22:50.535 --> 22:52.370
made from Falin's dragon parts?

22:53.205 --> 22:54.998
Or should we make a stew instead?

22:55.082 --> 22:57.125
- The broth from the bones--
- Stop it!

22:57.209 --> 23:00.087
Now's not the time
to be planning Falin menus!

23:01.088 --> 23:02.130
I'm hungry.

23:03.507 --> 23:05.008
Shall we prepare something?

23:05.092 --> 23:06.384
I second that!

23:07.052 --> 23:08.386
<i>Dungeon food.</i>

23:08.929 --> 23:10.847
<i>Eat or be eaten.</i>

23:11.515 --> 23:13.266
<i>There is no hierarchy.</i>

23:13.350 --> 23:17.145
<i>Eating is a privilege for those who live.</i>

23:17.979 --> 23:19.815
<i>Dungeon food.</i>

23:19.898 --> 23:22.484
<i>Oh, dungeon food.</i>

24:55.035 --> 24:56.870
Subtitle translation by: Ai Matsuoka
